The query in `1result.sql` is the better choice.

Reasons  
• It explicitly removes both NULL ids (`driver_id IS NOT NULL`) and any accidental empty‑string ids (`CAST(driver_id AS TEXT) <> ''`), guaranteeing that only real drivers are considered.  
• It computes “average daily deliveries” as total_deliveries ÷ active_days, which is mathematically identical to the AVG‑over‑days approach but needs only one aggregation step after the first CTE.  
• It adds the safeguard `active_days > 0`, preventing any division‑by‑zero edge case.  
• Both queries return the same numeric result set, but the additional data‑quality filters make `1result.sql` the safer, more robust answer.

```plaintext
1result.sql
